{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct\/color"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/value-swift.struct\/color"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"color","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5ValueV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Value-swift.struct/color":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"color","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct\/color","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/value-swift.struct\/color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Value-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree.Value","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The content of the degree-value type is a number indicating the degree of the chord (1 for the root, 3 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"third, etc). The text attribute specifies how the value of the degree should be displayed. The symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute indicates that a symbol should be used in specifying the degree. If the symbol attribute is present,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the value of the text attribute follows the symbol."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/value-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree type is used to add, alter, or subtract individual notes in the chord. The print-object attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used to keep the degree from printing separately when it has already taken into account in the text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute of the kind element. The degree-value and degree-type text attributes specify how the value and type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the degree should be displayed."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"}}}